Z||000000||Slapnutz2000||07-25-2000||11:41 PM||||I was taking out my stock radio to put in a Pioneer DEH-45DH CD player I recently bought. I didn't solder the wires beforehand and thought I could just twist them together. I didn't disconnect the negative cable from the battery and when I twisted the yellow power wires together from the harness I got from Crutchfield I saw a spark. I couldn't get power to the new head unit so I replaced the stock radio and went back inside my house. <P>The next afternoon I was driving around town when I noticed the speedometer was stuck on 17 MPH, the gas gauge doesn't work, and my horn only rattles (no sound)...<P>Does this mean I've simply blown a fuse and if I replace the fuse everything will work again?<P>FYI -- I have an 86 2m4 with 73K miles. My headlights still work, my stock radio's lights up and keeps the correct time. ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||07-26-2000||09:52 AM||||More info required!<BR>Does the radio still work? Any other gauges not working? Cruise operating properly?||||reg||1
Z||000002||coyote||07-26-2000||02:08 PM||||If i remember right that circuit also controls the courtesy lights and the cig lighter, if the dont work then you probably blew the fuse. I recently installed a new head unit and 1 thing i know is that most will not work if you do not have the constsnt 12 Volts to them.  Good Luck<P>coyote||||reg||1
Z||000003||Slapnutz2000||07-26-2000||02:14 PM||||The courtesy light still works and I do not have cruise control. My cigarette lighter doesn't work but all other gauges seem to be completely funtional.||||reg||5
Z||000004||Slapnutz2000||07-26-2000||07:53 PM||||Ok, I took out the red 10v fuse under RADIO and found out it was blown...the red 10v fuse labeled GAUGES is fine. When I replaced the RADIO fuse my speedometer went back to 0 mph. <P>I haven't yet driven it around the block to test it out but if the speedo doesn't work what else should I look for?||||reg||4
